==============================================================================
TWO TRIANGULAR TOWERS: COMPLETE SUBSET-FAMILY TAXONOMY  monad-S713
==============================================================================
The additive tower covers all positive integers because stage m is
  [m^2, ..., (m+1)^2-1] = A_L(m) union A_R(m).
The raw square shell does NOT: its stage-n carrier is
  [2n^2+n, ..., 2n^2+3n], length 2n+1,
and the gap before the next carrier has length 2n+2.

RAW SHELL COVERAGE
  n=1: shell=(3, 5), length=3, next gap=4
  n=2: shell=(10, 14), length=5, next gap=6
  n=3: shell=(21, 27), length=7, next gap=8
  n=4: shell=(36, 44), length=9, next gap=10
  n=5: shell=(55, 65), length=11, next gap=12
  n=6: shell=(78, 90), length=13, next gap=14
  n=7: shell=(105, 119), length=15, next gap=16
  n=8: shell=(136, 152), length=17, next gap=18

THE COMPLETE ENDPOINT-ALIGNED SUBSET FAMILIES
These are exactly the families where a B-endpoint lands on an A-half-endpoint.
There are 8 such families, one for each prefix/suffix choice in A_L/A_R.
  Exception: the Pell family BL prefix AR has a lone startup straddle (n,m)=(1,1),
  where B_L(1)=[3,4] starts at A_R(1)=[3] but spills one step into A_L(2)=[4].
  The genuine subset branch of that family starts at (3,4).

  BL prefix AL: [(4, 6), (144, 204), (4900, 6930)]
    Pell constants on first hits: [1, 1, 1]
    first hit meaning: n=4, m=6; subset of first 5 terms; tail deficit 2
  BL suffix AL: [(2, 3), (14, 20), (84, 119), (492, 696), (2870, 4059)]
    Pell constants on first hits: [-1, -1, -1, -1, -1]
    first hit meaning: n=2, m=3; subset of last 3 terms; head deficit 1
  BL prefix AR: [(3, 4), (39, 55), (109, 154), (1333, 1885), (3711, 5248)]
    Pell constants on first hits: [7, 7, 7, 7, 7]
    first hit meaning: n=3, m=4; subset of first 4 terms; tail deficit 0
  BL suffix AR: [(3, 4), (20, 28), (119, 168), (696, 984), (4059, 5740)]
    Pell constants on first hits: [-1, -1, -1, -1, -1]
    first hit meaning: n=3, m=4; subset of last 4 terms; head deficit 0
  BR prefix AL: [(3, 5), (20, 29), (119, 169), (696, 985), (4059, 5741)]
    Pell constants on first hits: [1, 1, 1, 1, 1]
    first hit meaning: n=3, m=5; subset of first 3 terms; tail deficit 3
  BR suffix AL: [(6, 9), (18, 26), (228, 323), (636, 900), (7770, 10989)]
    Pell constants on first hits: [7, 7, 7, 7, 7]
    first hit meaning: n=6, m=9; subset of last 6 terms; head deficit 4
  BR prefix AR: [(2, 3), (14, 20), (84, 119), (492, 696), (2870, 4059)]
    Pell constants on first hits: [-1, -1, -1, -1, -1]
    first hit meaning: n=2, m=3; subset of first 2 terms; tail deficit 1
  BR suffix AR: [(24, 34), (840, 1188)]
    Pell constants on first hits: [1, 1]
    first hit meaning: n=24, m=34; subset of last 24 terms; head deficit 10

THE USER'S EXAMPLES IN THIS TAXONOMY
  10+11+12 inside 9+10+11+12  -> BL suffix AL, first hit (n,m)=(2,3)
  13+14 inside 13+14+15      -> BR prefix AR, same Pell family (2,3)
  21+22+23+24                -> both BL prefix AR and BL suffix AR at (3,4)
                                so it is the unique exact shared B_L=A_R block
  25+26+27 inside 25+...+30  -> BR prefix AL, first hit (3,5)
  36+...+40 inside 36+...+42 -> BL prefix AL, first hit (4,6)

CONCISE PREDICTION RULE
  A family appears exactly when one of
    2n^2+n, 2n^2+2n, 2n^2+2n+1, 2n^2+3n
  equals one of
    m^2, m^2+m, m^2+m+1, m^2+2m.
  Each choice gives one Pell equation and therefore an infinite sparse family.
  The host size is m+1 in A_L(m), m in A_R(m);
  the guest size is n+1 for B_L(n), n for B_R(n).
  Their difference is the exact prefix/suffix deficit.

PELL FORMS
  BL prefix AL : 2n^2+n = m^2                 -> (4n+1)^2 - 8m^2 = 1
  BL suffix AL : 2n^2+2n = m^2+m             -> (2m+1)^2 - 2(2n+1)^2 = -1
  BL prefix AR : 2n^2+n = m^2+m+1            -> (4n+1)^2 - 2(2m+1)^2 = 7
  BL suffix AR : 2n^2+2n = m^2+2m            -> (2n+1)^2 - 2(m+1)^2 = -1
  BR prefix AL : 2n^2+2n+1 = m^2             -> 2m^2 - (2n+1)^2 = 1
  BR suffix AL : 2n^2+3n = m^2+m             -> (4n+3)^2 - 2(2m+1)^2 = 7
  BR prefix AR : 2n^2+2n+1 = m^2+m+1         -> (2m+1)^2 - 2(2n+1)^2 = -1
  BR suffix AR : 2n^2+3n = m^2+2m            -> (4n+3)^2 - 2(2m+2)^2 = 1
